 {:db/id "q-161906/ma-source-field/853602861505051cecf2b713626459834f93aa423fc63bf67d102c7a6f7ee5a1" :answer-field/id #uuid "8a4579ec-958a-5fd2-805d-97cd0da00894" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-161906/ma-source-field/853602861505051cecf2b713626459834f93aa423fc63bf67d102c7a6f7ee5a1/4f9ec97be1d62fe1de6febf810527f1e8a35b9dcb364e7445c843246d16c3651" "q-161906/ma-source-field/853602861505051cecf2b713626459834f93aa423fc63bf67d102c7a6f7ee5a1/bdb55ad0f6473f62ba59d76a4871960e4310fa80b386ac52e6bc46351dd153cd" "q-161906/ma-source-field/853602861505051cecf2b713626459834f93aa423fc63bf67d102c7a6f7ee5a1/ae15ea4a992f7aaa34a5a036b136a53783908b8339947a136dd94969f189337b" "q-161906/ma-source-field/853602861505051cecf2b713626459834f93aa423fc63bf67d102c7a6f7ee5a1/0a669fb2da4943876dc8b3df05652cf2872c8981b6fdd0b142cdabf0c1392799" "q-161906/ma-source-field/853602861505051cecf2b713626459834f93aa423fc63bf67d102c7a6f7ee5a1/2213f2d6244acdd375f023912de399b59e887030eb1bc4f095bce873ad15002b"] :answer-field/correct "q-161906/ma-source-field/853602861505051cecf2b713626459834f93aa423fc63bf67d102c7a6f7ee5a1/bdb55ad0f6473f62ba59d76a4871960e4310fa80b386ac52e6bc46351dd153cd" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-161906" :question/id #uuid "d8cd36a0-19ac-53de-ada3-7c525383dea4" :question/math-academy-id "q-161906" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F=⟨0,\\,x,\\,y⟩$ and the closed surface $S$ that encloses the finite region between the hemisphere $z=\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}$ and the plane $z=1-\\frac{1}{2}x.$ Let $D$ be the projection of $S$ onto the $xy$-plane. The flux of $F$ across $S$ can be expressed in terms of a double integral as \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∬}_{D}\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could be the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "Since we have a closed surface, the positive orientation is outward-pointing by convention. So,\n\n- the upper surface ${S}_{1}:z=g(x,y)=\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}$ is oriented upward, and\n\n- the lower surface ${S}_{2}:z=h(x,y)=1-\\frac{1}{2}x$ is oriented downward.\n\nNow, we write down the flux across each of the surfaces separately.\n\n- Consider the upper hemisphere ${S}_{1}.$\n\nWe compute the partial derivatives of $z=g(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}})=-\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}} \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}})=-\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we denote $F=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩,$ then\n\n$$\nP=0,\\,Q=x,\\,R=y.\n$$\n\n \n\nAs a result, since the positive orientation is upward, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{{S}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-0\\cdot (-\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}})-x\\cdot (-\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}})+y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{xy}{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}}+y)\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Consider lower plane ${S}_{2}.$ \n\nWe compute the partial derivatives of $z=h(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂h}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(1-\\frac{1}{2}x)=-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{∂h}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(1-\\frac{1}{2}x)=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we denote $F=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩,$ then\n\n$$\nP=0,\\,Q=x,\\,R=y.\n$$\n\n \n\nAs a result, since the positive orientation is downward, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{{S}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & =-{∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-{∬}_{D}(-0\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2})-x\\cdot 0+y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-{∬}_{D}y\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the flux across the entire surface is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{{S}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S+{∬}_{{S}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(\\frac{xy}{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}}+y)\\,\\text{d}A-{∬}_{D}y\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\frac{xy}{\\sqrt{4-{x}^{2}-{y}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-161906/ma-source-field/853602861505051cecf2b713626459834f93aa423fc63bf67d102c7a6f7ee5a1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
