 {:db/id "q-161913/ma-source-field/6a29bd131247cded16d49124894919f583cf1c23ef5110a758fa48bc1943b292" :answer-field/id #uuid "ae335d47-3b07-5474-9957-6ab74654f8ab" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-161913/ma-source-field/6a29bd131247cded16d49124894919f583cf1c23ef5110a758fa48bc1943b292/72df5251cc5107c08be1aa4f9ce08f1a0d24f10f9401abf5dc0f8f6ac91def26" "q-161913/ma-source-field/6a29bd131247cded16d49124894919f583cf1c23ef5110a758fa48bc1943b292/b94020f5be39b672763abdb52d864836008480beacf29599496658e91d04317f" "q-161913/ma-source-field/6a29bd131247cded16d49124894919f583cf1c23ef5110a758fa48bc1943b292/5a7c8c6ca9a2d0c7368b4ab28d9ee72b0ad8dc6fa7e00e509cdef67041d4924c" "q-161913/ma-source-field/6a29bd131247cded16d49124894919f583cf1c23ef5110a758fa48bc1943b292/fc80c17398065b660a228cad48b22af155be7c6739bb6a728a1b795eaa47b2df" "q-161913/ma-source-field/6a29bd131247cded16d49124894919f583cf1c23ef5110a758fa48bc1943b292/f66c1fc8a0f7c5f78f403ff74cddb7af549bfea70a115cadbc41c421591335a1"] :answer-field/correct "q-161913/ma-source-field/6a29bd131247cded16d49124894919f583cf1c23ef5110a758fa48bc1943b292/fc80c17398065b660a228cad48b22af155be7c6739bb6a728a1b795eaa47b2df" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-161913" :question/id #uuid "7b5db020-d92f-50c2-8c6b-3f44b9d6b975" :question/math-academy-id "q-161913" :question/problem "Consider the vector field $F=⟨{z}^{2},\\,0,\\,-x⟩$ and the closed surface $S$ that encloses the finite region between the cone $z=-\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}$ and the parabolic cylinder $z={y}^{2}-2.$ Let $D$ be the projection of $S$ onto the $xy$-plane. The flux of $F$ across $S$ can be expressed in terms of a double integral as \n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}F\\cdot dS={∬}_{D}\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following could be the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "Since we have a closed surface, the positive orientation is outward-pointing by convention. So,\n\n- the upper surface ${S}_{1}:z=g(x,y)=-\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}$ is oriented upward, and\n\n- the lower surface ${S}_{2}:z=h(x,y)={y}^{2}-2$ is oriented downward.\n\nNow, we write down the flux across each of the surfaces separately.\n\n- Consider the upper cone ${S}_{1}.$\n\nWe compute the partial derivatives of $z=g(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(-\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}})=-\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}} \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(-\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}})=-\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we denote $F=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩,$ then\n\n$$\nP={z}^{2}={x}^{2}+{y}^{2},\\,Q=0,\\,R=-x.\n$$\n\n \n\nAs a result, since the positive orientation is upward, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{{S}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\cdot (-\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}})-(0)\\cdot (-\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}})+(-x))\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(x\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}-x)\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Consider the lower cylinder ${S}_{2}.$ \n\nWe compute the partial derivatives of $z=h(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂h}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({y}^{2}-2)=0 \\\\ \\frac{∂h}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}-2)=2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we denote $F=⟨P,\\,Q,\\,R⟩,$ then\n\n$$\nP={z}^{2}={({y}^{2}-2)}^{2},\\,Q=0,\\,R=-x.\n$$\n\n \n\nAs a result, since the positive orientation is downward, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{{S}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & =-{∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂h}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂h}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-{∬}_{D}(-{({y}^{2}-2)}^{2}\\cdot (0)+0\\cdot (2y)+(-x))\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =-{∬}_{D}(-x)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}x\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the flux across the entire surface is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{{S}_{1}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S+{∬}_{{S}_{2}}F\\cdot \\text{d}S \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(x\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}-x)\\,\\text{d}A+{∬}_{D}x\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}x\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-161913/ma-source-field/6a29bd131247cded16d49124894919f583cf1c23ef5110a758fa48bc1943b292"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
