 {:db/id "q-32876/ma-source-field/c14d2c77c336fa72703d413816734746206e48a580d71d9f4990ec2a7a37d214" :answer-field/id #uuid "cc1f347e-fe06-5ef7-a082-5d1425a121dd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-32876/ma-source-field/c14d2c77c336fa72703d413816734746206e48a580d71d9f4990ec2a7a37d214/84c120f944673544abb22b46f0a3eddb0979089e85074f26bfe43f9d02af257b" "q-32876/ma-source-field/c14d2c77c336fa72703d413816734746206e48a580d71d9f4990ec2a7a37d214/6f0c31e9fdc37312e91107bdee65f61e455d0373551042027bcefb75a8b24b99" "q-32876/ma-source-field/c14d2c77c336fa72703d413816734746206e48a580d71d9f4990ec2a7a37d214/75537d91227eed77c3ad3e995d8298bde54228244402622900c92b89b62655fd" "q-32876/ma-source-field/c14d2c77c336fa72703d413816734746206e48a580d71d9f4990ec2a7a37d214/b7b09475f1f30c72dab4c0c42b933b5acbcdfb5a3e07be8240c87b8e1258d40a" "q-32876/ma-source-field/c14d2c77c336fa72703d413816734746206e48a580d71d9f4990ec2a7a37d214/10a099058ca09749d083f2614eff04aae533680cf7bf1b9594af2fbb5d5f745e"] :answer-field/correct "q-32876/ma-source-field/c14d2c77c336fa72703d413816734746206e48a580d71d9f4990ec2a7a37d214/75537d91227eed77c3ad3e995d8298bde54228244402622900c92b89b62655fd" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-32876" :question/id #uuid "33bfb8ae-51e5-575a-aee2-202f3434e957" :question/math-academy-id "q-32876" :question/problem "Which of the following gives the equation of the tangent to the curve $r(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t\\,j+t\\,k$ at the point $P(-1,0,\\frac{3}{2}),$ valid for real values of $u?$" :question/worked-solution "The point $P(-1,0,\\frac{3}{2})$ is at the tip of $r(t)$ for some specific value ${t}_{0}$ of the parameter $t.$ At this point,  the vector ${r}^{′}({t}_{0})$ is tangent to the curve, so the tangent line to the curve at $P$ can be parametrized as\n\n$$\nR(u)=r({t}_{0})+u\\,{r}^{′}({t}_{0}),\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\n \n\nFirst, we find the value of $t$ that corresponds to $P.$ We know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =-i+0\\,j+\\frac{3}{2}\\,k \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t\\,j+t\\,k & =-i+0\\,j+\\frac{3}{2}\\,k,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand equating the coefficients of $i,j,$ and $k$ yields the following system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t=-1 \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t=0 \\\\ t=\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get $t=\\frac{3}{2}.$ This value also satisfies the other two equations. Therefore, $P(-1,0,\\frac{3}{2})$ is at the tip of the vector $r(\\frac{3}{2}).$  \n\nWe calculate ${r}^{′}(t):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)\\,k \\\\  & =\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi t\\,i-\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi t\\,j+\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we evaluate ${r}^{′}(t)$ at $t=\\frac{3}{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(\\frac{3}{2}) & =\\pi \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})\\,i-\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})\\,j+\\,k \\\\  & =0\\,i+\\pi \\,j+\\,k \\\\  & =\\pi \\,j+\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the given curve at the point $P(-1,0,\\frac{3}{2})$ is\n\n$$\nR(u)=-i+\\frac{3}{2}\\,k+u\\,(\\pi \\,j+\\,k),\\,u\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-32876/ma-source-field/c14d2c77c336fa72703d413816734746206e48a580d71d9f4990ec2a7a37d214"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
