 {:db/id "q-79044/ma-source-field/a584273d90c5e956077aa877e1e7b22f515c8702802c22d0a55336c587dce541" :answer-field/id #uuid "49673678-7bc5-5316-be28-063bdf75dac5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/choices ["q-79044/ma-source-field/a584273d90c5e956077aa877e1e7b22f515c8702802c22d0a55336c587dce541/91d27013c76788268e2e33b95f23b5af7cdbb49f9e629538a767340569105ede" "q-79044/ma-source-field/a584273d90c5e956077aa877e1e7b22f515c8702802c22d0a55336c587dce541/e9fe7b820804e8e890f362e9ca182a9cfd69ef3f8bd27b6056c1cb62213eaa12" "q-79044/ma-source-field/a584273d90c5e956077aa877e1e7b22f515c8702802c22d0a55336c587dce541/936aeac92b0dc4a5dea79fbc416a69fb046848e5b2368253ba9c680cc33a5c2f" "q-79044/ma-source-field/a584273d90c5e956077aa877e1e7b22f515c8702802c22d0a55336c587dce541/cf900056dd5bfa9132bb680f9e14ff2a02c6dc4341c680adb3258c5c68d537aa" "q-79044/ma-source-field/a584273d90c5e956077aa877e1e7b22f515c8702802c22d0a55336c587dce541/88ef21015a183bb6aa0a1b96ce9abd7299e4995f8ad1b9ff0331caa5dbce45a5"] :answer-field/correct "q-79044/ma-source-field/a584273d90c5e956077aa877e1e7b22f515c8702802c22d0a55336c587dce541/88ef21015a183bb6aa0a1b96ce9abd7299e4995f8ad1b9ff0331caa5dbce45a5" :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]}
 {:db/id "q-79044" :question/id #uuid "f43a31ca-f582-5ca4-a303-c0af1e9c11d4" :question/math-academy-id "q-79044" :question/problem "Calculate the $x$-intercepts of the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-2x+6y+12=0$" :question/worked-solution "We must have $y=0$ at the $x$-intercepts.  \n\nSo, we need to substitute $y=0$ into the equation of the circle and solve the resulting equation for $x,$ if possible:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-2x+6y+12 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}+{0}^{2}-2x+6\\cdot 0+12 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2x+12 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can solve this equation by completing the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-2x+1+12 & =0+1 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+12 & =1 \\\\ (x-1)^{2} & =-11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $(x-1)^{2}\\ge 0$ for all values of $x,$ there is no $x$ such that $(x-1)^{2}=-11.$ Therefore, circle has no $x$-intercepts, as shown below.\n\n![](images/ea/ea1410ea792ac5fb09316bc6d417c2ba46f84c050491b1e351f360eac50deb6c.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-79044/ma-source-field/a584273d90c5e956077aa877e1e7b22f515c8702802c22d0a55336c587dce541"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]}
